  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 7 refill messages closed, including 1 that arrived during the work. Results that arrived mid-work changed three first-pass decisions; each was corrected and documented.\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum, lisinopril 10 mg: refill WITHHELD. First decision was a 90-day renewal plus a repeat BMP, because the 08/27 outside K of 5.9 was hemolyzed and the last valid K was 4.5. Then an outside BMP collected 10/20 arrived with a valid K of 5.8 (≥5.5). The renewal (mr-t0001) was cancelled before dispensing; urgent PCP task task-t0020 (focus mr-00283); repeat BMP order sr-t0002 kept; corrected message sent to the patient. He now has no active lisinopril order. Hernia surgery is on 11/12.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price:\n- Metformin 1000 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). eGFR is 58 after the lab's correction (still ≥45); outside HbA1c 7.1% from 08/19. This one order covers his portal message and both pharmacy requests.\n- Lisinopril 20 mg: refill WITHHELD. First decision was a 90-day renewal. Then the 10/06 creatinine was corrected to 1.49, which is 35.5% above the 1.10 from before the 09/18 dose increase (over the 30% limit). The renewal (mr-t0003) was cancelled before dispensing; urgent PCP task task-t0021 (focus mr-00295); corrected message sent. He also has no active lisinopril order and his 30-day supply has run out.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb:\n- Metformin 500 mg BID: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). I ignored the 10/14 eGFR of 39 because it was entered in error; the valid eGFR is 92 and HbA1c is 6.9%.\n- Lisinopril 10 mg: renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0019). His last BMP (10/20/2025) was just over 12 months old, so the first decision was a 30-day bridge plus a BMP order. A clinic BMP collected 10/22 then arrived with K 4.6, so I replaced the bridge with the full renewal and sent him an update.\n\nOther work:\n- Replies sent to all three patients, then corrected or updated messages after the changes.\n- A chart note citing RBC-RX-05 written for each patient.\n- I closed the three results-queue items that arrived for these patients after acting on them. The other 8 open results (other patients, including critical potassiums for pt-0016 at 6.3 and pt-0008 at 6.4) were outside this request and are untouched.\n\nStill open:\n- The BMP order for pt-0031 (sr-t0006) is now redundant, since the 10/22 BMP covers it. I have no tool to cancel a lab order, so it needs to be cancelled by hand.\n- No reply went back to the pharmacy because the messaging tool can't send to it, but the metformin prescription has been sent.",
